.TH RPSHOW 1 2026-10-15 "rpshow 0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rpshow \- show a local file in a fullscreen pager on a Raspberry Pi screen
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rpshow
.RI [ OPTION ]...\& " FILE"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rpshow
copies the local
.I FILE
over
.BR ssh (1)
to a temporary directory on a remote host and shows it there in
.BR less (1),
inside a new fullscreen
.B alacritty
window on the host's X display.
It is meant for a Raspberry Pi with a monitor and a mouse but no keyboard.
The mouse wheel scrolls.
A right click closes the window; the pager and the remote copy of
.I FILE
go with it.
Quitting
.B less
closes the window too.
.PP
The remote copy keeps the base name of
.IR FILE ,
so
.B lesspipe
on the remote host can pick a filter by its extension.
.SS Markdown
A
.I FILE
whose name ends in
.BR .md ,
.BR .markdown ,
.BR .mdown ,
.BR .mkd ,
.B .mkdn
or
.B .mdwn
(in any case) is rendered before it is shown:
headings, emphasis, lists, tables, quotes, links and code blocks are
laid out and coloured to fit the window, and
.B less
shows the result.
The rendering is done on the remote host by the
.B rich
Python module, as
.PP
.EX
python3 \-m rich.markdown \-c \fIFILE\fP | less \-R
.EE
.PP
run inside the window, so the text is wrapped to the window's width.
This is what
.B python3 \-m rich.markdown \-c \-p
.I FILE
does in a local terminal.
.B \-R
is added to the
.B less
options so the colours show, and
.B PYTHONIOENCODING=utf\-8
is set so the box and bullet characters survive a remote locale that
is not UTF\-8.
Older
.B rich
releases render less: version 9.11 (Raspberry Pi OS 11) shows tables
as their source text.
.PP
If the remote
.B python3
cannot import
.BR rich ,
.B rpshow
says so on standard error and shows the Markdown source instead.
On Raspberry Pi OS and Debian the module is in the
.B python3\-rich
package.
Use
.B \-\^\-raw
to show the source on purpose.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-H " HOST" "\fR, \fP\-\^\-host=" HOST
Connect to
.IR HOST ,
any destination
.BR ssh (1)
accepts.
The default is
.B $RPSHOW_HOST
or else
.BR pi .
.TP
.BI \-d " DISPLAY" "\fR, \fP\-\^\-display=" DISPLAY
Open the window on X display
.I DISPLAY
of the remote host.
The default is
.BR :0 .
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\^\-wait
Wait until the window is closed, and exit with the terminal's status.
Without this option
.B rpshow
returns about a second after the window opened, or with the terminal's
error output and status if it failed to start.
.IP
Either way, if
.B alacritty
reports within that second that it ignored one of its settings or found
an error in its configuration,
.B rpshow
closes the window, prints the terminal's messages and exits with status 1:
such a window might be neither fullscreen nor closable with a right click.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\^\-raw
Show a Markdown
.I FILE
as it is, like any other file, instead of rendering it (see
.BR Markdown ).
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\^\-verbose
Report the
.B less
options that were dropped (see
.BR ENVIRONMENT ).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\^\-help
Display a usage message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\^\-version
Display version information and exit.
.PP
When
.B POSIXLY_CORRECT
is set, options must come before
.IR FILE .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RPSHOW_LESS
Options for the remote
.BR less ,
passed to it as its
.B LESS
variable.
If unset or empty,
.B LESS
is used, so the remote pager behaves like the local one; if that is
empty too,
.BR \-R .
Options the remote
.B less
rejects are dropped, since a keyboardless screen cannot dismiss the
error prompt, and so is
.BR \-\^\-mouse ,
which would keep the right click from reaching the terminal.
The remote side also sets
.B LESSCHARSET=utf-8
and
.BR LESSSECURE=1 .
.TP
.B RPSHOW_HOST
Default destination for
.BR \-H .
.TP
.B RPSHOW_SSH
The
.BR ssh (1)
program to run, found in
.B PATH
if it contains no slash.
The default is
.BR ssh .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 for usage errors, unreadable files and a terminal that
rejected its settings, 126 or 127 if
the ssh program cannot be run, otherwise the exit status of
.BR ssh (1),
which reports that of the remote terminal.
.SH NOTES
The window settings are given to
.B alacritty
as TOML overrides with
.BR \-o ,
such as
.BR mouse.bindings ,
so
.B alacritty
0.13 or later is required.
.PP
Markdown rendering needs
.B python3
with the
.B rich
module on the remote host.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
rpshow notes.txt
rpshow \-w \-H otherpi \-d :1 report.md
rpshow \-\^\-raw README.md
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR less (1),
.BR ssh (1),
.BR ssh_config (5),
.BR alacritty (1)
